### Persons — /api/persons and /api/scopes/{scopeId}/…
#
# Run auth.http's "Login" first. A person is created through one of three endpoints depending on
# what they are: an administrator with no scope, a User inside a scope, or a new ScopeAdmin created
# directly as one of the scope's owners.
#
# "Create an administrator" stores the new person's id, which is what "Create a scope" in scopes.http
# uses as its initial owner. On a fresh database, run these two first, in that order.

### Create an administrator (UC-06 path b) — System Admin.
# No scope: role is 1 (SystemAdmin) or 2 (ScopeAdmin). A ScopeAdmin created here owns nothing yet.
POST {{host}}/api/persons
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Example Scope Admin",
  "email": "scope.admin@example.com",
  "password": "ChangeMe1!",
  "role": 2
}

> {%
    if (response.body.data && response.body.data.id) {
        client.global.set("personId", response.body.data.id);
        client.log("Stored personId " + response.body.data.id);
    }
%}

### Create a User in a scope (UC-06 path a) — System Admin or the owning Scope Admin.
# The role is implied: a person created here is always a User of this scope.
POST {{host}}/api/scopes/{{scopeId}}/persons
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Example User",
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "ChangeMe1!"
}

> {%
    if (response.body.data && response.body.data.id) {
        client.global.set("scopeUserId", response.body.data.id);
    }
%}

### Create a new Scope Admin directly as a co-owner (UC-06 path c) — System Admin or owning Scope Admin.
POST {{host}}/api/scopes/{{scopeId}}/owners
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Example Co-owner",
  "email": "co.owner@example.com",
  "password": "ChangeMe1!"
}

### Add an existing Scope Admin as an owner (UC-21) — System Admin or owning Scope Admin.
# No body: both identifiers are in the path. The person must already be a ScopeAdmin.
POST {{host}}/api/scopes/{{scopeId}}/owners/{{personId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Promote a scope's User to owner (UC-23) — System Admin or owning Scope Admin.
# The person must be a User of this scope; the promotion makes them a ScopeAdmin who owns it.
POST {{host}}/api/scopes/{{scopeId}}/users/{{scopeUserId}}/promote
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Read one person (UC-07) — any authenticated caller; a person may always read themselves.
GET {{host}}/api/persons/{{personId}}?includeDeleted=false
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List a scope's Users (UC-07) — System Admin or owning Scope Admin.
# Owners are not Users and do not appear here — use the listing below for those.
GET {{host}}/api/scopes/{{scopeId}}/persons?pageNumber=1&pageSize=20&includeDeleted=false
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List a scope's owners (UC-07) — System Admin or owning Scope Admin.
GET {{host}}/api/scopes/{{scopeId}}/owners?pageNumber=1&pageSize=20&includeDeleted=false
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update a person (UC-08) — any authenticated caller, subject to the handler's rules.
# roleId may only be changed by a System Admin; omit it entirely for a self-service name/email edit.
PUT {{host}}/api/persons/{{personId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Example Scope Admin, renamed",
  "email": "scope.admin@example.com"
}

### Remove an owner from a scope (UC-22) — System Admin or owning Scope Admin.
# Refused if it would leave the scope with no owner.
DELETE {{host}}/api/scopes/{{scopeId}}/owners/{{personId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Logically delete a person (UC-09) — System Admin or owning Scope Admin.
DELETE {{host}}/api/persons/{{personId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Hard delete a person (UC-10) — System Admin.
# Irreversible, and cascades to the applications they own, their tokens, their 2FA configuration and
# their join rows.
DELETE {{host}}/api/persons/{{personId}}/hard
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
